 "sourceMesh": "artifacts/homm3_mesh_surgery/h3_boar_rider_hand_c1.glb",
 "meshSurgeryReason": "2026-10-11 lane D (standing mesh-surgery approval): the Meshy mesh welds the resting right fist and mace onto the boar's mane (56 bridge faces), so the DEF g12 mace swing (overhead, wound back, swung down in front) tore a mane shard out with the fist (patch gate: 2018 -> 2067 edges over 2x; a weight re-solve tore more, 2234). limb_cut_surgery.py (on a scratch copy of the source carrying the delivery skin) splits the bridge by majority and duplicates the 28 shared vertices; every original vertex, face, UV and texel is unchanged.",
 "strideMatch": {
  "highHarmonicKeep": 0.7,
  "reason": "2026-10-11 lane D: after the hand_c1 limb cut (fist + mace off the mane) the rebuilt raw Move measures jitter p90 0.034, but the stride-matched (plant) Move reads 0.369 (worst FR2; cap 0.35), so fleet_rebuild refused it as a new articulation:jittery fault. k 0.7 gives p90 0.282 (worst FR2 0.553) with slipRatio 0.160 (prior delivery 0.112) and requiredOverActual 1.120 (1.074); no gate faults in a scratch run of the delivery stages"
 },
 "glbPatch": {
  "reason": "2026-10-11 lane D authenticity: DEF g12 AttackFront mace swing - mace raised overhead (f0), wound back behind the shoulder (f1), overhead again (f2), swung forward (f3) and down in front of the boar's snout (f4), recovering at f5; the delivered swing barely left the shoulder. RightArm/RightForeArm aims per frame, split over two keyRotations ops. Death needs no patch (rider slumps, boar rears at f3-f4 already).",
  "ops": [
   {
    "op": "setWeights",
    "table": "tools/homm3_glb_patch/key_rotations/h3_boar_rider_hand_split.json",
    "sha256": "9979332933da79336122db296031e88f90fd400bd363c7fa1da5a885362e6cfe",
    "note": "fist/mace vs mane contact after the hand_c1 limb cut: the build's heat skin bleeds RightHand/RightForeArm weight onto the mane and WolfBody/WolfNeck/Hips weight onto the fist across the open cut; geodesic split (45 to the arm, 15 to the body)"
   },
